  <data name="Performance.Report.Boundary" xml:space="preserve"><value>This is observation, not a stress test. Crossing a threshold or coinciding with a marker does not prove the cause of a failure. Statistics use available samples, not a share of elapsed time; unavailable and missed values are not replaced with zero. CPU is the average between GetSystemTimes readings, RAM is physical memory, and disks are WMI PhysicalDisk _Total (100 − PercentIdleTime and current queue), not only the system volume. Metrics are read sequentially rather than atomically; WMI has its own refresh interval. Collection and other software can affect load. The health index is not changed.</value></data>
